---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { emails, site } from '../data/site';

const toc = [
  { id: 'who-we-are', title: '1. Who we are' },
  { id: 'what-we-collect', title: '2. What we collect' },
  { id: 'tiktok', title: '3. TikTok data' },
  { id: 'how-we-use', title: '4. How we use data' },
  { id: 'legal-bases', title: '5. Legal bases' },
  { id: 'retention', title: '6. Storage and retention' },
  { id: 'sub-processors', title: '7. Sub-processors' },
  { id: 'cookies', title: '8. Cookies and tracking' },
  { id: 'your-rights', title: '9. Your rights' },
  { id: 'deletion', title: '10. Deleting your account' },
  { id: 'security', title: '11. Security' },
  { id: 'children', title: '12. Children' },
  { id: 'platforms', title: '13. Platform policies' },
  { id: 'changes', title: '14. Changes' },
  { id: 'contact', title: '15. Contact' },
];
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How Postmonster handles your data: what we collect (account, content, connected channels), why, how long we keep it, your rights and how to delete your account."
  canonicalPath="/privacy"
  toc={toc}
>
  <p class="note">
    This policy is written in plain language and is a working document for Early Access.
    It is reviewed and signed off by the operator. Effective date: {site.effectiveDate}.
  </p>

  <h2 id="who-we-are">1. Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    Postmonster is operated by {site.legalName} ({site.country}), contact
    <a href={`mailto:${emails.privacy}`}>{emails.privacy}</a>. In this policy, "we", "us"
    and "Postmonster" refer to this service and its operator; "you" refers to the user of
    the service or visitor of {site.url}.
  </p>

  <h2 id="what-we-collect">2. What we collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Account data:</strong> your name, email address, password (stored hashed) and
      workspace membership.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Access requests:</strong> if you request Early Access, we store the details
      you submit — name, email, role, main networks, team size and what you want to use
      Postmonster for — plus the request status.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Content:</strong> the posts you write and schedule, and the images or videos
      you upload to the media library.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Connected channels:</strong> for each network you connect, the identifiers of
      the account (such as display name, username and avatar URL) and the access tokens
      needed to publish on your behalf. Disconnecting a channel deletes its tokens.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Operational data:</strong> publishing results and statuses, error messages
      from networks, and basic service logs needed to run and secure the service.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Communications:</strong> emails you send us and the replies.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We do not buy contact lists and we do not enrich your profile with data from
    third-party brokers.
  </p>

  <h2 id="tiktok">3. TikTok data</h2>
  <p>
    When you connect a TikTok account through TikTok's Content Posting API, we receive and
    store: your TikTok open_id, display name and username, profile picture URL, the OAuth
    access and refresh tokens, and the identifiers and statuses of the posts you publish
    (publish_id and status).
  </p>
  <p>
    We do not store your TikTok videos outside the content you upload for scheduling, and
    we do not collect follower analytics or other audience data. Tokens are used only to
    publish the posts you create. Disconnecting the TikTok channel revokes and removes the
    tokens immediately.
  </p>

  <h2 id="how-we-use">4. How we use data</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Provide the service: scheduling, publishing, status tracking, previews.</li>
    <li>Send transactional emails: account activation, invites, publishing failures, replies.</li>
    <li>Review Early Access requests and onboard small batches.</li>
    <li>Keep the service secure: abuse prevention, rate limiting, incident investigation.</li>
    <li>Comply with legal obligations.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We do not use your content to train models and we do not sell personal data.</p>

  <h2 id="legal-bases">5. Legal bases</h2>
  <p>
    Where the GDPR applies, we rely on: performance of a contract (providing the service
    you signed up for), legitimate interests (security, abuse prevention, improving
    reliability), consent (where we ask for it — for example receiving non-essential
    emails), and legal obligation (accounting and law-enforcement requests).
  </p>

  <h2 id="retention">6. Storage and retention</h2>
  <p>
    We keep account and content data while your account is active. Publishing history is
    kept with your workspace so you can audit what went out. When you delete your account,
    we delete personal data and content without undue delay; access tokens are removed
    immediately, and residual copies in backups age out within 30 days. Access requests
    that do not convert to accounts are kept for up to 12 months (or less on request), so
    we can follow up and avoid duplicates.
  </p>

  <h2 id="sub-processors">7. Sub-processors</h2>
  <p>
    We use a small set of sub-processors to run the service:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Hosting:</strong> the server operator providing the compute and storage.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Email delivery:</strong> a transactional email provider for activation,
      invites and notifications.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Networks you connect:</strong> content is delivered to the platforms you
      choose (TikTok, YouTube, etc.) under their own terms and privacy policies.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    The current list is available on request at
    <a href={`mailto:${emails.privacy}`}>{emails.privacy}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="cookies">8. Cookies and tracking</h2>
  <p>
    This website ({site.url}) uses no cookies, no analytics and no third-party trackers.
    The application (app.postmonster.xyz) uses a session cookie that is strictly necessary
    to keep you logged in.
  </p>

  <h2 id="your-rights">9. Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Subject to applicable law, you can request access to your personal data, correction,
    deletion, export (data portability), restriction or objection, and withdraw consent
    where processing is consent-based. Write to
    <a href={`mailto:${emails.privacy}`}>{emails.privacy}</a> — we answer within 30 days.
    You can also lodge a complaint with your local data protection authority.
  </p>

  <h2 id="deletion">10. Deleting your account</h2>
  <p>
    You can delete your account yourself in Settings (account deletion requires typing
    your email to confirm). This removes your profile, workspaces you solely own,
    connected channel tokens (revoked first), media, posts and scheduling data. If you
    share a workspace with other members, you can leave the workspace and the owner keeps
    the team content. A confirmation email is sent either way.
  </p>

  <h2 id="security">11. Security</h2>
  <p>
    Traffic is encrypted in transit (HTTPS). Access to production data is limited to the
    operator, and access tokens for connected channels are stored for use by the service
    only. No system is perfect: if we learn of a breach affecting your data, we will
    notify you and the competent authorities as required by law.
  </p>

  <h2 id="children">12. Children</h2>
  <p>
    Postmonster is not directed at children. You must be at least 16 (or the minimum age
    required in your country, e.g. 13 in the US) to use the service. If you believe a
    child has given us personal data, contact us and we will delete it.
  </p>

  <h2 id="platforms">13. Platform policies</h2>
  <p>
    When you connect third-party networks, their own policies apply to the data they
    process — for example the
    <a href="https://www.tiktok.com/legal/privacy-policy" rel="noopener nofollow" target="_blank"
      >TikTok Privacy Policy</a
    >, the
    <a
      href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy"
      rel="noopener nofollow"
      target="_blank">Google API Services User Data Policy</a
    > for YouTube and Google, and Meta's policies for Instagram and Facebook. Our use of
    data received from those platforms is limited to the purposes described here.
  </p>

  <h2 id="changes">14. Changes</h2>
  <p>
    If this policy changes materially, we will update this page and note the new effective
    date. For material changes that affect your rights, we will notify account holders by
    email.
  </p>

  <h2 id="contact">15. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Privacy questions, data requests and complaints:
    <a href={`mailto:${emails.privacy}`}>{emails.privacy}</a>. General contact:
    <a href={`mailto:${emails.hello}`}>{emails.hello}</a>. Operator: {site.legalName},
    {site.country}.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
